\section{Discussion}

Qwen achieves the strongest results, particularly under zero-shot English prompting. LLaMA exhibits higher output variability, while DeBERTa captures surface-level relevance but struggles with implicit causal reasoning.

\section{Next Steps}

We plan to extend our system with structured and multi-expert reasoning:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Hybrid LLM–encoder systems
    \item RLHF-style feedback for explanation ranking
    \item Retrieval-enhanced multi-expert ensembles
\end{itemize}

\section{Conclusion}

This interim report highlights the challenges of abductive event reasoning under noisy evidence conditions. Our results suggest that large instruction-tuned models provide strong baselines, with further gains expected from hybrid and structured reasoning approaches.

